## Story DD Coverage
- dd-5: orchestrator dispatches all 9 applier leaves (inbound_create/update/delete/clean_label/repair_property/probe + outbound_create/update/delete) (sc-1)

## Testing Mode
RED

## DISPATCH GATE (plan-review F2)
Sprint MUST verify cde1-30ba status=closed BEFORE dispatching T4. T4 imports cde1's Action enum (the 9-leaf taxonomy source-of-truth). Without cde1, the coverage test cannot enumerate the action set. Pre-dispatch check:
```bash
.claude/scripts/dso ticket show cde1-30ba-d186-48d2 | jq -e '.status == \"closed\"' || echo 'FAIL: cde1 still open'
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Unit tests pass (exit 0)
  Verify: pytest -xvs tests/unit/dso_reconciler/test_dispatch_coverage.py
- [ ] Lint passes (exit 0)
  Verify: make lint-ruff
- [ ] Format check passes (exit 0)
  Verify: make format-check
- [ ] Enumerative coverage: every (direction, action) pair in {inbound, outbound} × cde1.Action is either dispatched to an applier OR explicitly in reconcile.INVALID_PAIRS — union equals full cartesian product
  Verify: pytest -xvs tests/unit/dso_reconciler/test_dispatch_coverage.py::test_all_direction_action_pairs_covered
- [ ] All 9 named leaves route to distinct appliers (no duplicates)
  Verify: pytest -xvs tests/unit/dso_reconciler/test_dispatch_coverage.py::test_each_leaf_routes_to_distinct_applier
- [ ] Unknown (direction, action) pair raises NotImplementedError naming the tuple
  Verify: pytest -xvs tests/unit/dso_reconciler/test_dispatch_coverage.py::test_unknown_pair_raises_named_not_implemented
- [ ] T3's main() tests continue to pass after dispatch table integration (regression guard per plan-review F6)
  Verify: pytest -xvs tests/unit/dso_reconciler/test_reconcile_main.py

## Implementation Notes

Add to plugins/dso/scripts/dso_reconciler/reconcile.py:

```python
INVALID_PAIRS: set[tuple[str, str]] = set()  # populated only if cde1's Action enum has pairs that don't apply both directions

def _dispatch_mutation(mutation, context):
    d, a = mutation.direction, mutation.action
    # inbound branches
    if d == 'inbound' and a == 'create':
        from .applier import inbound_create; return inbound_create(mutation, context)
    if d == 'inbound' and a == 'update':
        from .applier import inbound_update; return inbound_update(mutation, context)
    if d == 'inbound' and a == 'delete':
        from .applier import inbound_delete; return inbound_delete(mutation, context)
    if d == 'inbound' and a == 'clean_label':
        from .applier import inbound_clean_label; return inbound_clean_label(mutation, context)
    if d == 'inbound' and a == 'repair_property':
        from .applier import inbound_repair_property; return inbound_repair_property(mutation, context)
    if d == 'inbound' and a == 'probe':
        from .inbound_probe import probe; return probe(mutation.target)
    # outbound branches
    if d == 'outbound' and a == 'create':
        from .applier import outbound_create; return outbound_create(mutation, context)
    if d == 'outbound' and a == 'update':
        from .applier import outbound_update; return outbound_update(mutation, context)
    if d == 'outbound' and a == 'delete':
        from .applier import outbound_delete; return outbound_delete(mutation, context)
    raise NotImplementedError(f'no dispatch arm for (direction={d!r}, action={a!r})')
```

Wire _dispatch_mutation into reconcile_once so each emitted mutation flows through it. Lazy imports per branch preserve T3's 'no module-top fetcher/applier loading' invariant.

The coverage test imports cde1's Action enum and enumerates {inbound, outbound} × Action; for each pair, either (a) calls _dispatch_mutation with a synthetic Mutation and asserts no NotImplementedError, OR (b) asserts the pair is in INVALID_PAIRS. Union must equal full cartesian product.

## Retry Budget
MAX_ATTEMPTS: 3 (sonnet model)
On 3 consecutive sonnet failures: escalate to opus with full diagnostic context (all 3 failure messages)
On 3 consecutive opus failures (6 total): escalate to user with full failure history
If MAX_AGENTS: 0 at sonnet→opus escalation time: skip opus step, escalate to user immediately
